Scheduled Task

[Screenshot – Scheduled Task keyword search]

The search identified scheduled-task activity involving cmd.exe and notepad.exe.

2. Scheduled Task Creation

A scheduled task was observed that was created to execute cmd.exe, which subsequently executes notepad.exe.

The observed process command line was:

C:\Windows\system32\cmd.exe /C schtasks /create /F /tn \Microsoft\Windows\SoftwareProtectionPlatform\EventCacheManager /tr "C:\Windows\system32\cmd.exe /C C:\Windows\System32\notepad.exe" /sc ONSTART /ru system /S

[Screenshot – Scheduled Task creation and process command line]

The scheduled task was created with the following configuration:

Task Name: Microsoft\Windows\SoftwareProtectionPlatform\EventCacheManager
Execution: cmd.exe
Child Process: notepad.exe
Schedule: ONSTART
Run As: SYSTEM
Parameter: /S

The /sc ONSTART parameter configures the task to execute when the system starts.

The /ru system parameter configures the task to run under the SYSTEM account.

The /S parameter is relevant when investigating scheduled-task operations involving a specified system.

