9. Conclusion

The investigation identified a scheduled task configured to execute cmd.exe, which subsequently executed notepad.exe under the SYSTEM account.

Additional events showed handle duplication, library loading, and network communication between 172.16.39.5 and 172.16.39.6 over ports 135 and 49671.

Based on the correlation of the scheduled-task activity and network communication between the two systems, the activity indicates possible lateral movement using Scheduled Task/Job.

Further evidence such as authentication events, the originating account, destination-host task creation events, and parent-child process relationships would help confirm whether the activity represents actual remote lateral movement.
